    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nFix routed-expert output boundaries for multimodal requests whose model-side prompt expands placeholder tokens into longer ranges.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Preserve all R3 routed-expert rows covering model-expanded multimodal prompts.\n- Clamp `routed_experts_prompt_start` to the effective expanded prompt boundary.\n- Keep text-only request behavior unchanged.\n- Add regression coverage for multimodal expansion and P/D prompt cuts\n\n## Validation\n\nDirect connector assertions for expanded multimodal bounds and P/D prompt-cut clamping passed.\n\n## Details\n\nRequest.num_prompt_tokens and Request.num_tokens can describe compact client-side token IDs, while the model executes expanded multimodal placeholder ranges from mm_features. The auxiliary-output connector previously used the compact lengths for routed-expert metadata and final slicing, which could drop or misalign image-expanded routing rows.\n\nThe fix derives effective model-side prompt and total lengths from multimodal placeholder ranges, uses those lengths for connector metadata and output slicing, and preserves the existing text-only path.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [ ] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [ ] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n\n",
